      <guid isPermaLink="false">3dd21fb6140b71c7f76476d8</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:00:20 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>An intensifying crisis in Germany’s auto industry has triggered a high-stakes battle over one of the most prized entitlements its factory workers have: the 35-hour work week. Executives at Mercedes-Benz Group AG said last week they’re halting domestic investments, and plant closures could be next, if employees don’t agree to work more. They’re reportedly insisting on three extra hours of labor per week with no additional pay.</description>
